I. Execution Organs and Their Functions

1. A People's Court shall, as needed and in accordance with the relevant provisions of laws, establish an execution organ to be specifically responsible for execution work.

2. The execution organ shall be responsible for executing the following effective legal instruments:
(1) civil and administrative judgments, rulings, and mediation agreements of the People's Court, civil sanction decisions, payment orders, as well as criminal incidental civil judgments, rulings, and mediation agreements, and the property-related parts of criminal judgments;
(2) administrative penalty decisions and administrative handling decisions that shall be executed by the People's Court according to law;
(3) arbitration awards and mediation agreements rendered by arbitration institutions of China, and rulings on property preservation and evidence preservation made by the People's Court in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Arbitration Law of the People's Republic of China;
(4) notarized creditor's rights documents to which the notary organ has given compulsory execution effect according to law;
(5) judgments and rulings made by foreign courts whose effects have been recognized by rulings of the People's Court, as well as arbitration awards made by foreign arbitration institutions;
(6) other legal instruments that laws provide shall be executed by the People's Court.

3. Rulings on property preservation and advance execution made by the People's Court in the course of trying civil and administrative cases shall generally be transferred to the execution organ for implementation.

4. For cases concluded by the people's tribunal, the people's tribunal shall be responsible for execution. Among them, complex or difficult cases, or cases where the person subject to execution is not within the jurisdiction of the court, shall be executed by the execution organ.

5. Major matters in the execution proceedings shall be discussed by more than three execution officers and reported to the president of the court for approval.

6. The execution organ shall be equipped with necessary means of transportation, communication equipment, audio-visual equipment, and police equipment, so as to ensure timely and effective performance of its duties.

7. When performing official duties, execution personnel shall show their work identification to the relevant persons and dress in accordance with the regulations. When necessary, judicial police shall participate.

8. The execution organ of a superior People's Court shall be responsible for the supervision, guidance, and coordination by the court of the execution work of lower People's Courts.

10. Application of Compulsory Measures Against Acts Obstructing Enforcement
57. Where a party subject to enforcement or any other person commits any of the following acts of refusing to perform an effective legal instrument or obstructing enforcement, the People's Court may handle the matter in accordance with the provisions of Article 111 of the Civil Procedure Law:
(1) concealing, transferring, selling, or destroying the property provided to the People's Court as security for enforcement;
(2) an outsider maliciously colluding with the party subject to enforcement to transfer the property of the party subject to enforcement;
(3) intentionally tearing up the enforcement announcement or seals of the People's Court;
(4) forging, concealing, or destroying important evidence concerning the performance ability of the party subject to enforcement, thereby obstructing the People's Court from ascertaining the property status of the party subject to enforcement;
(5) instigating, bribing, or coercing another person to give false testimony on issues concerning the property status and ability to perform obligations of the party subject to enforcement;
(6) obstructing the People's Court from conducting a lawful search;
(7) obstructing or resisting enforcement by violence, threat, or other means;
(8) making a disturbance or storming the enforcement site;
(9) insulting, slandering, framing, besieging, threatening, assaulting, or retaliating against the enforcement personnel of the People's Court or the personnel assisting in enforcement;
(10) damaging or seizing enforcement case materials, official enforcement vehicles, other enforcement equipment, uniforms of enforcement personnel, and official enforcement credentials.
58. Where, during the enforcement process, a party subject to enforcement or any other person refuses to perform an effective legal instrument or obstructs enforcement under serious circumstances and criminal liability needs to be investigated, the relevant materials shall be transferred to the relevant authorities for handling.
